Package: bayesreml
Title: Bayesian Mixed Models with ASReml Syntax, Powered by Greta
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("AAGI", "University of Adelaide", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "aagi@adelaide.edu.au"),
    person("Claude", "Anthropic", role = "ctb",
           comment = "AI-assisted development")
    )
Description: Specify mixed models using familiar ASReml formula syntax and
    estimate them via Bayesian MCMC using 'greta'. Returns results in formats
    compatible with the standard R modelling ecosystem including 'summary()',
    'emmeans', 'marginaleffects', and 'effectsize'. The package translates
    ASReml-style formulas (fixed, random, rcov) to efficient greta code using
    an indexing approach that scales to large agricultural datasets. Supports
    Gaussian, binomial, Poisson, negative binomial, gamma, and beta families,
    as well as structured covariance models (us, fa, ar1), genomic relationship
    matrices (GBLUP), pedigree-based models, spatial models, and splines.
